# Git line-ending policy.
#
# Shell scripts MUST be checked out with LF. The Keycloak bootstrap script
# (docker/keycloak/import/entrypoint.sh) is bind-mounted into the container
# and executed by `sh`: with CRLF line endings the shell reads a stray
# carriage return as part of the command, so the script dies with
# "set: -r: invalid option" before it ever substitutes the secrets - and the
# whole compose stack fails to boot Keycloak.
#
# `text eol=lf` overrides the local core.autocrlf setting, so the file is LF
# in every working tree regardless of the platform.

# The rule is deliberately limited to the shell scripts: widening it to the
# YAML or JSON files would rewrite hundreds of unrelated files and invalidate
# the source-audit reviews of files that never changed.

*.sh text eol=lf

# Windows batch files are binary for Git's line-ending purposes: the cmd.exe
# parser needs CRLF and the file must not be rewritten on checkout.
*.cmd -text
*.bat -text
